product harness under test.\n- Treat `multi-agent-logs/` as imported historical progress/evidence.\n- For a possible BYO-Firmware-MCP defect, first preserve and classify the reproducer under `run-firmware-test-suite`. Only a manager-verified production-code defect may enter the direct `$plan-changes` then `$change-loop` repair route.\n- Fresh firmware doers may inspect only their assigned `fresh-experiments/<run>/` worktree and its explicitly copied inputs. They may not inspect the catalog, product harness, server source, or another run.\n- Do not operate hardware without a current user instruction authorizing hardware testing and a matching recorded scope in `.agent-workspace/USER_DELEGATED_AUTHORIZATION.md`.\n\nWait — the firmware suite rules say \"Do not read files above `Firmware/` when planning, launching, reviewing, or resuming the suite.\" But the AGENTS.md context from above Firmware/ was included in my context. The rule says don't read files above Firmware/ — I should respect that and not read files above Firmware/.\n\nAlso, the current working directory is `C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\fresh-experiments\\S11_20260821-plan2-suite-013`.\n\nLet me start by reading the required files:\n1. `README.md` (in Firmware/)\n2. `PROVIDER_ADAPTER.md` (in Firmware/)\n3. `.codex/skills/run-firmware-test-suite/SKILL.md`\n4. The selected section of `BYO_FIRMWARE_MCP_END_TO_END_EXPERIMENTS.md`\n\nAlso the `.agent-workspace/` in the current run directory has:\n- `CONTINUATION_PROMPT_002_POLICY_BOUND.md`\n- `CONTINUATION_PROMPT_002.md`\n- `INITIAL_MANIFEST.json`\n- `RESOURCE_ASSIGNMENT.md`\n- `RESULT.schema.json`\n- `REVIEWER_PROMPT_POLICY_BOUND.md`\n- `REVIEWER_PROMPT.md`\n- `RUN_STATE.json`\n- `SPEC_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW.md`\n- `SPEC.md`\n- `suite013_reviewer_s11_002_codex.jsonl`\n- `suite013_reviewer_s11_002_controller.status.json`\n- `suite013_reviewer_s11_002.stderr.log`\n- `suite013_reviewer_s11_replacement_003_codex.jsonl`\n- `suite01