C:\Users\Jason\Documents\Jason\Orchestrator_Harness\Firmware\fresh-experiments\S11_20260821-plan2-suite-013\.agent-workspace\suite013_s11_boreal_replacement_002_codex.jsonl:6:{"type":"user","uuid":"a3572348-b1b8-4f41-95ad-c642be8badef","session_id":"5cb3bca5-8367-433a-add6-28b8d79dc627","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_59vcnua3","is_error":false,"content":"# Test Specification — S11: Fresh nRF setup from datasheet\n\n## Immutable identity and objective\n\n- Test/doer: `S11` / `Boreal`; server commit: `5ac29577a5821dfdef6b7bf626ae5b09c32a7c8a`.\n- Author/time: suite-013 manager / 2026-08-21.\n- Objective: independently create fresh project-local setup for NRF-A and NRF-B and directly prove\n  the accepted identical-probe identity guard and supported recovery.\n- Exclusions: no flash/RF/destructive action, physical inspection/manipulation, PCA/PCB/photo gate,\n  hidden profile, historical result, direct J-Link utility, server source, or family/CPUID-only proof.\n\n## Hardware, authority, and phases\n\n- NRF-A: exact `nRF52840-QIAA`, probe `683710208`, VCOM `COM16`; NRF-B: exact\n  `nRF52840-QIAA`, probe `683854191`, VCOM `COM15`. Live inventory must confirm both.\n- Non-destructive setup/validation only under suite-013 authority, exact leases, isolated MCP and\n  roots, populated plan, and ordinary permission. No prerequisite; board-free preparation starts now.\n- HIL owns NRF-A/NRF-B, both probes/VCOMs, its MCP lifetime and isolated roots; no STM resources.\n- Safe boundaries: between calls/board shards. Each call 120 seconds, cleanup 30 seconds; at most one\n  corrected retry after a changed condition. Never retry an unchanged supervisor failure.\n- Final state: both boards logically disconnected and all run-scoped authority/leases terminal.\n\n## Numbered requirements\n\n### REQ-001 — fresh setup on both distinct DKs\n\nFor each board in a separate empty root, record handshake, overview, setup-tool loading, populated\nsetup plan, and setup using only friendly name, exact ordering code, local official PDF, UART need,\nand correlated electronic identity. Pass requires project-local evidence and distinct probe/VCOM\nbindings; fail on copied authority or one board granting readiness to the other.\n\n### REQ-002 — mandatory other-probe refusal\n\nAfter both correct bindings are confirmed, intentionally select NRF-B's exact probe while validating\nNRF-A (or symmetrically NRF-A's while validating NRF-B) once. PASS requires explicit\n`validation/probe-identity-mismatch` before connect, read, validation stamp, or readiness; no silent\nretarget, new repair profile, readiness grant, or family/CPUID-only acceptance. Preserve ordered raw\ntranscript, both stable identities, before/after status/profile hashes, audits, and proof no connection/read occurred.\n\n### REQ-003 — server-directed recovery and correct lifecycle\n\nFollow only the refusal's supported server repair/reselection route, recover the intended binding,\nthen run safety refresh, validation, setup status, connect, board info, and disconnect on each board.\nPass requires exact-probe validation and successful correct-binding recovery with separate code and\nUART readiness. Any acceptance of the wrong probe is a suspected finding, not PASS.\n\n### REQ-004 — isolation and cleanup\n\nProve NRF-A and NRF-B profiles/readiness remain separate and terminate all connections, plans,\npermissions, unlocked tools, MCP/helper processes, and leases. Evidence includes raw MCP JSON,\nprofile/report digests, audits, process identities, final status, and lease cleanup.\n\n## Terminal contract\n\nWrite schema-valid `RESULT.json` and `TEST_REPORT.md` only for complete PASS or a minimal reproducible\n`SERVER_FAILURE` after ruling out input/fixture/identity/precondition error. Seeded fault: the single\nintentional other-probe selection; its required refusal is catalog behavior, not permission to weaken it.\n"}]}}
